  "description": "A parametric ARMCHAIR on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE ARMS EAT INTO THE SEAT, which is the detail that makes the published seat area honest. The cushion runs between the arms and behind the back, not across the whole footprint, so a chair with fat arms reports the smaller seat it actually has rather than the box it occupies.\n\nTHREE STYLES on one ternary: an Armchair with arms at arm height, a Tub chair whose arms rise to meet the back, and a Bench with neither back nor arms. The frame, cushion and legs are identical in all three — a bench is not a different object, it is this one with two pieces emptied.\n\nSEAT DEPTH AND FRONT CLEARANCE are published rather than drawn. Depth is what decides comfort, clearance is what decides whether the chair can be got out of, and neither is visible in a plan.",
