            {
              "id": "modelling_plan",
              "name": "Modelling plan (for Blender / engine agents)",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "ARMCHAIR — MODELLING PLAN (surface draft; to be refined)\nMetres unless stated; values in braces are this object's parameters. Z up, floor at Z 0. Hosted on a point: origin at the placement point on the floor.\n\nWHAT IT IS\nmid-century armchair, boucle upholstery, walnut splayed legs\n\nGEOMETRY\nModel the object described above as clean, closed meshes with real thickness and small bevels on exposed edges (about 2 mm) so highlights catch. Drive every dimension from these parameters:\n- Width: {length}\n- Depth: {width}\n- Back height: {height}\n- Seat height: {seatHeight}\n- Cushion thickness: {seatThk}\n- Back thickness: {backThk}\n- Arm width: {armWidth}\n- Arm height: {armHeight}\n- Leg height: {legHeight}\n- Style: {style} (one of: Armchair / Tub chair / Bench (no back))\n- Rotation (deg): {rotation}\n- Anchor Direction: {anchorDir} (one of: Top-Left / Top-Center / Top-Right / Left-Center / Center / Right-Center / Bottom-Left / Bottom-Center / Bottom-Right)\n- Margin from host: {margin}\n- Flip side: {flipSide}\nKeep the proportions of a well-made real product; add the secondary detail a close-up render needs (joints, reveals, fixings) but no hidden interior geometry.\n\nMATERIALS\n- Base colour: {baseColor}\n- Roughness: {roughness}\nPrincipled BSDF per visible part, using the colour and roughness above for the main surface; secondary parts in a neutral complementary finish. Use Object / box-projected texture coordinates (no UVs needed). Add a subtle noise bump (strength ~0.03) so surfaces are not perfectly flat.\n\nLIGHTS\nNone. This object does not emit light.\n\nCHECKS (measure after building)\n- Width = {length}\n- Depth = {width}\n- Back height = {height}\n- Seat height = {seatHeight}\n- Arm width = {armWidth}\n- Arm height = {armHeight}\n- Leg height = {legHeight}\n- All meshes closed, no duplicate faces, origin as stated above.",
